          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people the answer is one small bottle of Goo Gone Original for stickers and labels, and the habit of washing the surface afterwards. Step up to Pro-Power for aged tape, use 3M 08984 on cured car paint, and keep Un-Du for paper and glass. If fumes or painted walls are the worry, start with Motsenbocker's Lift Off and accept a slower job.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Floors are a different purchase. Buy a gallon of Sentinel 747 Plus or Blue Bear 500MR, budget time for dwell and rinsing, and let the floor dry before new flooring goes down. Above all, treat old black mastic as a testing problem before it is a removal problem: test it, keep it wet, and never sand it.
